    <section class="reasons-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><p class="eyebrow">Quick answers</p><h2 id="faq-title">Common questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can individual actions really help?</summary><p>Yes, especially when they become shared habits and support better systems. Personal choices can reduce demand, build community, and show leaders what people value.</p></details><details><summary>What makes an action high impact?</summary><p>Start with actions that reduce fossil-fuel use, protect nature, improve resilience, or help more people participate. The best action is one you can sustain and invite others into.</p></details><details><summary>Where should I begin?</summary><p>Pick one area you care about: energy, transport, food, nature, or community education. Our projects page turns those interests into practical ways to get involved.</p></details></div></section>
